W AX3051 391-restrict-effect-transparent.ax:59:6-11 restriction-unverifiable "`viaIo` claims `restrict(no-io)` and the claim cannot be checked: the body CALLS its own parameter `f`, so what it performs is decided by the argument each caller passes - the effect row is complete about this body and says nothing about that call" ?"a limit of the ANALYSIS rather than a defect in the program - AX3037's argument at one remove. There are three readings: an effect present only as POSSIBLE, a row the walk marked incomplete, and a body that CALLS one of its own parameters (`#effect-params=`), whose answer is chosen by each caller and cannot be settled here at all. Name the function at the call, stop calling the parameter, or drop the claim; `no-cast` and `no-wrap` are checked regardless, because both are lexical and need no call resolved"
